   "text": {
    "L1": "In a race, everyone covers the same distance. The smaller time wins.",
    "L2": "A bigger time is not always better; in a race it means the runner took longer.",
    "L3": "To compare timings, first use the same unit. One minute is 60 seconds, so 1 minute 5 seconds is 65 seconds.",
    "L4": "Compare stopwatch times place by place. 12.45 seconds is less than 12.50 seconds, so 12.45 is faster.",
    "L5": "The difference tells how much faster the winner was. From 38.6 to 39.1 seconds is 0.5 seconds.",
    "L6": "So Rina wins when she runs 200 metres in 38.6 seconds and Tara takes 39.1 seconds.",
    "L7": "Now order these race times from fastest to slowest."
   },
